// madcide — the madc IDE (hub doc Phase 2; Track 7.2's consumer).
// Usage: madc tools/madcide/madcide.mad <file> [ro]
// Run it from the repository root (verb bodies and keybinding profiles
// load by relative path). The buffer is the texteditor machinery; the
// diagnostics pane and outline are projections of live compiler data;
// keybindings are configurable profiles — the full JOE/WordStar set by
// default (see profiles/joe.keys, the readable truth: WordStar diamond
// ^B^F^P^N + ^A/^E + ^Z/^X words + ^U/^V screens; ^K S/^K D save ·
// ^K X save+exit · ^K Q quit · ^C discard · ^K B/^K K block begin/end ·
// ^K C/^K M/^K Y block copy/move/delete · ^K F find + ^L find next ·
// ^_ undo / ^^ redo · ^Y/^W delete line/word · ^K R insert file ·
// ^K L go to line · ^K U/^K V file top/end · ^K H help (the loaded
// profile, projected) · ^K Z shell · ^K E edit file (buffers, JOE's
// own key; open path switches, missing path = New File) · ^K ; check ·
// ^T options (live values, Keymap row swaps profiles) · ^K I outline ·
// ^K O/^K N/^K P split/next/previous window · ^K A cycle the code view
// original/MC11/C11 — plus C++ (the reverse render) on a C/C++ buffer —
// the view seam: read-only lenses over the one document · ^N the MODES
// palette (owner 2026-08-31): ":" inside it — @modes profile data —
// enters the vi colon line (:w :q :N :e file :!cmd ...), "v" toggles vi
// MODAL editing (modes-as-scopes: @normal/@insert scope data + the
// count/operator grammar; profiles/neovim.keys is the modal personality
// and loads in normal mode)),
// Pico-style single chords in the pico profile.
// The buffer holds a persistent parse handle (madc::parse_open at load,
// whole-TU refresh on check/save/outline); the status line shows the
// enclosing function from its RETAINED state — composition never runs
// the compiler. Syntax colour rides the same handle: madc::parse_spans
// classification through a colour SCHEME (profiles/*.theme — class ->
// JOE-vocabulary style spec, data like the keybindings; ^K T swaps
// schemes by name), refreshed with the parse.
// Tab cycles focus (buffer / pane / menu); a pane row chosen with enter
// moves the caret to its line.
// The gateway seam (design doc 2026-08-31): madcide_core.inc is the
// SESSION layer (class IdeSession — state + semantics, terminal-free);
// madcide_client.inc is the TUI CLIENT (the only tui-handle holder:
// render/input/refresh/suspend + the run_ide loop).
#include "../texteditor/lined_core.inc"
#include "../texteditor/editor_events.inc"
#include "madcide_core.inc"
#include "madcide_client.inc"

int main(int argc, char **argv)
{
    if ( argc < 2 )
    {
	printf("usage: madcide <file> [ro]\n");
	return 1;
    }
    run_ide(argv[1], argc > 2);
    return 0;
}
